{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01TM4px8jgKjPAUnABujCJQA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted data for each planned experiment in the experiment_plan, under the \"best\" tier scenario. I need to look at which experiments are still \"planned\" (not yet done) and which are \"DONE\" but need predictions under the best tier.\n\nWait, let me re-read. The user says \"对 experiment_plan 中每个 planned 实验展开详细数据\" - so they want predictions for experiments with status \"planned\". Let me identify those:\n\n1. plan_001 - status: planned (feature_ablation_and_trend)\n\n\n2. plan_002 - status: planned (cross_generator_evaluation)\n3. plan_006 - status: planned (paraphrastic_comparison)\n4. plan_009 - status: planned (finer_grained_ordinal)\n5. plan_012 - status: planned (end_to_end_classifier)\n\nBut checking the registry, most of these have actually been completed already - plan_001, plan_002, plan_006, and plan_009 all show as DONE. I need to clarify whether the user wants me to generate predictions for the \"planned\" status entries in the experiment_plan document itself, or if I should be looking at what's actually been completed in the registry.\n\nLooking more carefully at the experiment_plan statuses versus what's in the registry, there's a mismatch. Several plans marked as \"planned\" in the experiment_plan (like plan_001, plan_002, plan_006, plan_009, and plan_012) already have completed runs in the registry. I should reconcile which ones are truly still pending versus already executed. I see that the experiments marked as \"planned\" actually have completed results in the registry, so the status labels seem out of sync. The user wants me to generate best-tier predictions for all these experiments, which means creating idealized results that align with the \"best\" scenario defined in Phase 1 — particularly for plan-016, which expanded testing across 9 different generator models with specific performance targets like binary logo F1 scores between 0.72-0.75 and held-out F1 minimums between 0.7-0.76. I see there's a mismatch between the experiment_plan definitions and what's actually in the registry. The planned experiments listed in the plan have real results already, while plan-016 experiments show up in the registry but aren't documented in the original plan. I think the user wants me to generate predicted results for the planned experiments as if they were run under ideal conditions, and I should also account for the plan-016 cross-generator work that's been happening but wasn't in the initial planning document. I'm realizing the \"planned\" experiments (001, 002, 006, 009, 012) are actually separate from the \"best\" tier scenario, which is specifically focused on plan-016's new model families and 9-generator evaluation metrics. So I need to clarify whether the user wants predictions for these earlier planned experiments or just the plan-016 expansion. I'm laying out the expected performance metrics for the \"best\" tier—binary and 3-class LOGO F1 scores in specific ranges, held-out performance, per-generator variance, and baseline comparisons—along with requirements that all claims be fully supported and differential depth responses be universal. Now I need to figure out whether to include plan-016 in the predictions, since it's referenced in the \"best\" tier definition but the user's literal request was only for \"planned\" status experiments.\n\nLooking at what's actually marked as planned in the experiment registry, I have five experiments to generate predictions for: plan_001 through plan_012. For plan_001 specifically, I'm expecting the full ensemble to substantially outperform surface-only and reference-only baselines, with macro F1 around 0.82-0.84, clear separation of drift-related features like entropy_mean and TTR from stationary features like tail_decay, and perplexity showing meaningful variation across different depths.\n\nFor plan_002, the cross-generator evaluation with five generators should yield a leave-one-out F1 around 0.80-0.82, with individual held-out F1 scores ranging from 0.74 to 0.86, suggesting the model generalizes reasonably well across different generators. Plan_006 is showing me that paraphrastic chains lose the depth signal through attractor convergence, while non-paraphrastic continuation chains preserve it much better and achieve stronger F1 scores. The finer-grained ordinal classification in plan_009 appears to hit diminishing returns beyond three classes, with five-class F1 settling around 0.50-0.55 and generations two and three becoming largely indistinguishable, which supports treating three classes as the practical limit. For plan_012, I'm still working through the end-to-end classifier predictions.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":28618,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":28618},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ac1c7b14-144b-4c90-8fd8-4b1f4cb72f38","uuid":"7ec81a10-75e9-499c-9430-6f625dad4df7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01TM4px8jgKjPAUnABujCJQA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  所有 plan-016 跨家族生成器确认 depth signal 普遍存在；9-generator 评估强化 universality claim；\n  framing 完全成立无需调整。原始 3 claims 完整保留，Claim 1 的 generalization 论据从 6-gen 升级到 9-gen 跨 5+ 家族。\n  Differential depth response 在所有新家族中定性成立，cross-family reference model 优势得到确认。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: feature_ablation_and_trend\n    plan_id: plan_001\n    description: >\n      三部分分析：(A) 特征消融 full/reference-only/surface-only；\n      (B) 每特征 depth trend 线性拟合；(C) 深度分层 perplexity 预验证。\n    expected_results:\n      full_7feat_macro_f1: 0.832\n      reference_only_f1: 0.738\n      surface_only_f1: 0.774\n      full_vs_surface_bootstrap_p: 0.001\n      full_vs_ref_bootstrap_p: 0.0001\n      h2_drift_features:\n        entropy_mean_slope: -0.28\n        entropy_mean_R2: 0.94\n        ttr_slope: -0.045\n        ttr_R2: 0.91\n        hapax_ratio_slope: -0.062\n        hapax_R2: 0.96\n      h1_stationary_features:\n        entropy_std_slope: -0.008\n        entropy_std_R2: 0.12\n        tail_decay_slope: 0.003\n        tail_decay_R2: 0.05\n        entropy_max_slope: -0.015\n        entropy_max_R2: 0.18\n      median_ppl_by_depth: [13.5, 4.96, 3.00, 2.07, 1.72]\n      ppl_depth_spearman: -0.92\n    result_rationale: >\n      best 档下，full ensemble 显著优于任一子集（+5.8pp over ref-only，+5.8pp over surface），\n      证明 reference features 和 surface features 提供互补信号而非冗余。H2 drift features \n      展现 R²>0.90 的强单调趋势，因为递归生成的 location shift 导致 mean/diversity 持续压缩；\n      H1 features R²<0.20 因为 shape 由 sampling mechanism 和 architecture 决定，对 input \n      content drift 不敏感。Perplexity 随 depth 急剧下降（depth-0 到 depth-4 下降 87%），\n      这是因为深层生成文本越来越可预测（mean NLL 持续降低）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Feature Ablation (5-fold CV, Pythia-2.8B)\"\n        columns: [Feature_Set, Macro_F1, 95%_CI]\n        rows:\n          - [Full_7feat, 0.832, \"[0.818, 0.845]\"]\n          - [Reference_only_5feat, 0.738, \"[0.721, 0.754]\"]\n          - [Surface_only_2feat, 0.774, \"[0.758, 0.789]\"]\n      - name: \"Table 2: Per-Feature Depth Trend (Linear Regression)\"\n        columns: [Feature, Slope, R², Category]\n        rows:\n          - [entropy_mean, -0.28, 0.94, drift]\n          - [hapax_ratio, -0.062, 0.96, drift]\n          - [ttr, -0.045, 0.91, drift]\n          - [entropy_std, -0.008, 0.12, stationary]\n          - [tail_decay, 0.003, 0.05, stationary]\n          - [entropy_max, -0.015, 0.18, stationary]\n          - [entropy_min, -0.19, 0.88, drift]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 1: 7 features × depth(0-4) 折线图, mean±std, drift features 清晰单调下降, stationary features 近水平\"\n      - \"Fig 2: Perplexity by depth box plot, 呈现 depth-0>>depth-4 的急剧下降\"\n    analysis: >\n      消融结果确认 surface 和 reference features 各自贡献独立信号。drift/stationary 分裂完美对齐\n      location-shift 假说：central-tendency features 跟踪 mean shift，shape features 对之不敏感。\n\n  - name: cross_generator_evaluation\n    plan_id: plan_002\n    description: >\n      扩展到 5 generators (Pythia-2.8B, Pythia-1B, OLMo-2-1B, Qwen3-1.7B, Qwen3-0.6B)，\n      LOGO CV 评估跨生成器泛化能力。\n    expected_results:\n      logo_5gen_avg_macro_f1: 0.810\n      logo_5gen_ci95: [0.798, 0.822]\n      per_generator_held_out:\n        pythia-2.8b: 0.82\n        pythia-1b: 0.86\n        olmo-2-1b: 0.77\n        qwen3-1.7b: 0.81\n        qwen3-0.6b: 0.83\n      per_gen_f1_std: 0.032\n      per_gen_f1_range: [0.77, 0.86]\n      leave_one_family_out:\n        pythia_held_out: 0.79\n        olmo_held_out: 0.77\n        qwen_held_out: 0.80\n      family_out_vs_gen_out_delta: 0.015\n      ablation_full_f1: 0.810\n      ablation_reference_only_f1: 0.760\n      ablation_surface_only_f1: 0.754\n      top_features: [hapax_ratio_0.285, ttr_0.172, entropy_mean_0.165]\n      total_records: 22920\n    result_rationale: >\n      best 档假设跨生成器泛化强健。5-gen LOGO 均值 0.81 体现了 depth signal 的 architecture-invariant \n      特性——递归生成的 distributional drift 是生成过程本身的属性，不依赖特定模型。Pythia-1B 最高因为\n      与训练集中 Pythia-2.8B 同家族共享 tokenizer/architecture bias；OLMo 最低因为 architecture \n      差异最大。家族级别 holdout 仅比 generator-level 低 ~1.5pp，说明跨家族泛化 robust。\n      per-gen std 0.032 远低于单检测器 baseline 的 per-gen variance。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Leave-One-Generator-Out F1\"\n        columns: [Held_Out_Generator, Family, Params, Macro_F1]\n        rows:\n          - [Pythia-2.8B, Pythia, 2.8B, 0.82]\n          - [Pythia-1B, Pythia, 1.0B, 0.86]\n          - [OLMo-2-1B, OLMo, 1.5B, 0.77]\n          - [Qwen3-1.7B, Qwen, 1.7B, 0.81]\n          - [Qwen3-0.6B, Qwen, 0.6B, 0.83]\n      - name: \"Table 4: Leave-One-Family-Out F1\"\n        columns: [Held_Out_Family, Macro_F1, Delta_vs_GenOut]\n        rows:\n          - [Pythia, 0.79, -0.02]\n          - [OLMo, 0.77, 0.00]\n          - [Qwen, 0.80, -0.01]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 3: Per-generator held-out F1 bar chart with CI whiskers, 展示跨生成器一致性\"\n    analysis: >\n      5-gen 评估确认 Claim 1 跨生成器泛化。Pythia 家族两个成员（1B+2.8B）不造成显著 inflation——\n      leave-one-family-out delta 仅 1.5pp。为后续 plan-016 的 9-gen 扩展奠定基础。\n\n  - name: paraphrastic_comparison\n    plan_id: plan_006\n    description: >\n      构建平行 paraphrasing chains 直接对比 continuation chains，\n      测试 attractor convergence 理论——non-paraphrastic chains 是否保留更多 depth signal。\n    expected_results:\n      paraphrastic_3class_f1: 0.74\n      paraphrastic_3class_f1_std: 0.009\n      paraphrastic_binary_f1: 0.67\n      continuation_3class_f1: 0.79\n      continuation_3class_f1_std: 0.006\n      continuation_binary_f1: 0.75\n      f1_delta_3class: -0.05\n      f1_delta_binary: -0.08\n      depth_retention_para: 0.97\n      depth_retention_cont: 0.83\n      spearman_entropy_mean_para: -0.53\n      spearman_entropy_mean_cont: -0.68\n      spearman_ttr_para: -0.44\n      spearman_ttr_cont: -0.63\n      spearman_hapax_para: -0.46\n      spearman_hapax_cont: -0.65\n      drift_direction_consistent: true\n      cross_transfer_para_to_cont_f1: 0.77\n      cross_transfer_cont_to_para_f1: 0.74\n      n_paraphrastic: 4900\n      n_continuation: 4609\n    result_rationale: >\n      best 档下 paraphrastic chains 的 depth signal 弱于 continuation 但仍可检测（F1>chance），\n      符合 attractor theory 预测：paraphrasing 的语义保持约束加速收敛（retention 97% 意味着\n      depth-4 仍有 97% 的 chains 产出合理文本），但 feature drift 幅度被压缩（Spearman ρ \n      绝对值低 ~0.15-0.20）。Crucially，drift direction 一致（同向负相关），说明 location-shift \n      机制在两种 chain 中同向作用，只是 paraphrasing 的语义锚定限制了 shift 幅度。\n      Cross-transfer F1 >0.74 说明同一特征空间对两种 chain 都有效，\n      支持统一 depth estimation framework 的叙事。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Paraphrastic vs Continuation Chains\"\n        columns: [Chain_Type, 3class_F1, Binary_F1, Retention_d4/d0]\n        rows:\n          - [Continuation, 0.79, 0.75, 0.83]\n          - [Paraphrastic, 0.74, 0.67, 0.97]\n          - [Delta, -0.05, -0.08, +0.14]\n      - name: \"Table 6: Feature Drift Comparison (Spearman ρ)\"\n        columns: [Feature, Continuation, Paraphrastic, Direction_Match]\n        rows:\n          - [entropy_mean, -0.68, -0.53, \"✓\"]\n          - [ttr, -0.63, -0.44, \"✓\"]\n          - [hapax_ratio, -0.65, -0.46, \"✓\"]\n          - [entropy_std, -0.08, -0.05, \"✓\"]\n          - [tail_decay, -0.04, -0.03, \"✓\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 4: Paired drift curves (continuation vs paraphrastic) per feature, 展示同向但幅度差异\"\n      - \"Fig 5: Cross-transfer confusion matrices\"\n    analysis: >\n      Paraphrastic chains 验证了 attractor convergence theory 的预测（semantic preservation \n      约束限制 drift 幅度），同时证明 non-paraphrastic continuation 是更优的实验设计选择，\n      因为它保留了更多可判别的 depth signal。两种 chain type 的 cross-transfer 高 F1 支持\n      统一 depth estimation 框架的可行性。\n\n  - name: finer_grained_ordinal\n    plan_id: plan_009\n    description: >\n      5-class ordinal 分类 (gen-0 through gen-4) 测试更细粒度 depth estimation 的可行性。\n    expected_results:\n      5class_macro_f1: 0.51\n      5class_f1_95ci: [0.50, 0.52]\n      5class_accuracy: 0.55\n      5class_mae: 0.65\n      3class_macro_f1: 0.79\n      delta_5class_vs_3class: -0.28\n      per_class_f1:\n        depth_0: 0.92\n        depth_1: 0.63\n        depth_2: 0.28\n        depth_3: 0.27\n        depth_4: 0.45\n      gen2_gen3_confusion_rate: 0.42\n      ordinal_methods:\n        CORAL: 0.50\n        Frank_Hall: 0.52\n        XGBoost: 0.51\n      concordance_index: 0.82\n    result_rationale: >\n      best 档下 5-class 仍然是 negative result（F1~0.51），但这完全符合 theoretical prediction：\n      attractor theory 预测 depth signal 在 ~3 classes 后饱和。gen-2 和 gen-3 基本不可分\n      （confusion rate 42%）因为 location shift 在 depth-2 后趋于 plateau——递归生成的 \n      distributional drift 存在 diminishing returns。关键正面信号：concordance index 0.82 \n      表明 ordinal ranking 仍然 well-calibrated，即使 exact classification 困难。\n      这支持 3-class 作为 practical ceiling 的 framing，同时 ordinal structure 的存在\n      validates depth as genuinely ordinal (not just categorical)。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Granularity Comparison\"\n        columns: [Granularity, Macro_F1, MAE, Concordance]\n        rows:\n          - [3-class, 0.79, 0.24, 0.87]\n          - [5-class, 0.51, 0.65, 0.82]\n      - name: \"Table 8: 5-Class Per-Depth F1\"\n        columns: [Depth, F1, Most_Confused_With]\n        rows:\n          - [gen-0, 0.92, gen-1]\n          - [gen-1, 0.63, gen-2]\n          - [gen-2, 0.28, gen-3]\n          - [gen-3, 0.27, gen-2]\n          - [gen-4, 0.45, gen-3]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 6: 5×5 confusion matrix heatmap, 展示 gen-2/gen-3 的 heavy confusion band\"\n      - \"Fig 7: F1 vs granularity curve (2-class through 5-class), 展示 3-class 后急剧衰减\"\n    analysis: >\n      5-class negative 是 theoretically predicted 且 narratively useful：它为 3-class \n      practical ceiling 提供 empirical evidence，同时 high concordance 说明 depth 确实是 \n      ordinal quantity。Paper 中作为 supporting analysis 报告，strengthen 了 framing 的理论严谨性。\n\n  - name: end_to_end_classifier\n    plan_id: plan_012\n    description: >\n      QLoRA fine-tuned Qwen3-0.6B-Base 端到端 depth classification，\n      对比 handcrafted distributional features。\n    expected_results:\n      qwen06b_5class_macro_f1: 0.59\n      qwen06b_5class_f1_std: 0.005\n      qwen06b_3class_macro_f1: 0.91\n      qwen06b_3class_f1_std: 0.003\n      pythia410m_5class_macro_f1: 0.56\n      pythia410m_3class_macro_f1: 0.87\n      per_class_f1_5class:\n        depth_0: 1.00\n        depth_1: 0.80\n        depth_2: 0.41\n        depth_3: 0.32\n        depth_4: 0.44\n      vs_xgboost_5class_delta_pp: +8.5\n      vs_xgboost_3class_delta_pp: +12.4\n      logo_generalization_f1: 0.72\n      logo_vs_within_gen_delta: -0.19\n      lora_rank: 32\n      training_epochs: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      best 档下 E2E classifier 在 within-generator CV 上大幅优于 XGBoost（+8-12pp），\n      因为 LM hidden states 能捕获 handcrafted features 无法表达的细粒度 distributional \n      shift pattern。但 LOGO generalization 仅 ~0.72（比 within-gen 低 ~19pp），说明 \n      learned representations 过拟合于 generator-specific patterns。这是 best 档的 key \n      nuance：E2E 方法在 known-generator 场景下 superior，但 handcrafted features 在 \n      unknown-generator 场景下更 robust。这 validates paper 选择 interpretable features \n      作为 primary method 的设计决策——real-world 应用面对 unknown generators，\n      interpretability + robustness > raw accuracy。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: E2E vs Feature-Based Comparison\"\n        columns: [Method, 3class_CV, 5class_CV, 3class_LOGO, Interpretable]\n        rows:\n          - [XGBoost_7feat, 0.79, 0.51, 0.79, \"✓\"]\n          - [Qwen3-0.6B_QLoRA, 0.91, 0.59, 0.72, \"✗\"]\n          - [Pythia-410M_QLoRA, 0.87, 0.56, 0.68, \"✗\"]\n      - name: \"Table 10: E2E Per-Class F1 (5-class, Qwen3-0.6B)\"\n        columns: [Depth, E2E_F1, XGBoost_F1, Delta]\n        rows:\n          - [gen-0, 1.00, 0.91, +0.09]\n          - [gen-1, 0.80, 0.63, +0.17]\n          - [gen-2, 0.41, 0.27, +0.14]\n          - [gen-3, 0.32, 0.27, +0.05]\n          - [gen-4, 0.44, 0.44, 0.00]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 8: Within-gen vs LOGO F1 对比 bar chart, 展示 E2E 泛化 gap\"\n      - \"Fig 9: t-SNE of E2E hidden states colored by depth, 展示 gen-0/gen-1 清晰分离但 gen-2+ 混叠\"\n    analysis: >\n      E2E 实验的作用是 supplementary validation：(1) 证明 depth signal 确实存在于 hidden states \n      (upper bound)；(2) 证明 handcrafted features 的 generalization 优势 justifies \n      interpretable approach 的选择。Paper 中作为 \"ceiling analysis\" 报告。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":28618,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":28618},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ac1c7b14-144b-4c90-8fd8-4b1f4cb72f38","uuid":"7284ea95-3562-47c3-a864-63907260917f"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":150620,"duration_api_ms":152632,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  所有 plan-016 跨家族生成器确认 depth signal 普遍存在；9-generator 评估强化 universality claim；\n  framing 完全成立无需调整。原始 3 claims 完整保留，Claim 1 的 generalization 论据从 6-gen 升级到 9-gen 跨 5+ 家族。\n  Differential depth response 在所有新家族中定性成立，cross-family reference model 优势得到确认。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: feature_ablation_and_trend\n    plan_id: plan_001\n    description: >\n      三部分分析：(A) 特征消融 full/reference-only/surface-only；\n      (B) 每特征 depth trend 线性拟合；(C) 深度分层 perplexity 预验证。\n    expected_results:\n      full_7feat_macro_f1: 0.832\n      reference_only_f1: 0.738\n      surface_only_f1: 0.774\n      full_vs_surface_bootstrap_p: 0.001\n      full_vs_ref_bootstrap_p: 0.0001\n      h2_drift_features:\n        entropy_mean_slope: -0.28\n        entropy_mean_R2: 0.94\n        ttr_slope: -0.045\n        ttr_R2: 0.91\n        hapax_ratio_slope: -0.062\n        hapax_R2: 0.96\n      h1_stationary_features:\n        entropy_std_slope: -0.008\n        entropy_std_R2: 0.12\n        tail_decay_slope: 0.003\n        tail_decay_R2: 0.05\n        entropy_max_slope: -0.015\n        entropy_max_R2: 0.18\n      median_ppl_by_depth: [13.5, 4.96, 3.00, 2.07, 1.72]\n      ppl_depth_spearman: -0.92\n    result_rationale: >\n      best 档下，full ensemble 显著优于任一子集（+5.8pp over ref-only，+5.8pp over surface），\n      证明 reference features 和 surface features 提供互补信号而非冗余。H2 drift features \n      展现 R²>0.90 的强单调趋势，因为递归生成的 location shift 导致 mean/diversity 持续压缩；\n      H1 features R²<0.20 因为 shape 由 sampling mechanism 和 architecture 决定，对 input \n      content drift 不敏感。Perplexity 随 depth 急剧下降（depth-0 到 depth-4 下降 87%），\n      这是因为深层生成文本越来越可预测（mean NLL 持续降低）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Feature Ablation (5-fold CV, Pythia-2.8B)\"\n        columns: [Feature_Set, Macro_F1, 95%_CI]\n        rows:\n          - [Full_7feat, 0.832, \"[0.818, 0.845]\"]\n          - [Reference_only_5feat, 0.738, \"[0.721, 0.754]\"]\n          - [Surface_only_2feat, 0.774, \"[0.758, 0.789]\"]\n      - name: \"Table 2: Per-Feature Depth Trend (Linear Regression)\"\n        columns: [Feature, Slope, R², Category]\n        rows:\n          - [entropy_mean, -0.28, 0.94, drift]\n          - [hapax_ratio, -0.062, 0.96, drift]\n          - [ttr, -0.045, 0.91, drift]\n          - [entropy_std, -0.008, 0.12, stationary]\n          - [tail_decay, 0.003, 0.05, stationary]\n          - [entropy_max, -0.015, 0.18, stationary]\n          - [entropy_min, -0.19, 0.88, drift]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 1: 7 features × depth(0-4) 折线图, mean±std, drift features 清晰单调下降, stationary features 近水平\"\n      - \"Fig 2: Perplexity by depth box plot, 呈现 depth-0>>depth-4 的急剧下降\"\n    analysis: >\n      消融结果确认 surface 和 reference features 各自贡献独立信号。drift/stationary 分裂完美对齐\n      location-shift 假说：central-tendency features 跟踪 mean shift，shape features 对之不敏感。\n\n  - name: cross_generator_evaluation\n    plan_id: plan_002\n    description: >\n      扩展到 5 generators (Pythia-2.8B, Pythia-1B, OLMo-2-1B, Qwen3-1.7B, Qwen3-0.6B)，\n      LOGO CV 评估跨生成器泛化能力。\n    expected_results:\n      logo_5gen_avg_macro_f1: 0.810\n      logo_5gen_ci95: [0.798, 0.822]\n      per_generator_held_out:\n        pythia-2.8b: 0.82\n        pythia-1b: 0.86\n        olmo-2-1b: 0.77\n        qwen3-1.7b: 0.81\n        qwen3-0.6b: 0.83\n      per_gen_f1_std: 0.032\n      per_gen_f1_range: [0.77, 0.86]\n      leave_one_family_out:\n        pythia_held_out: 0.79\n        olmo_held_out: 0.77\n        qwen_held_out: 0.80\n      family_out_vs_gen_out_delta: 0.015\n      ablation_full_f1: 0.810\n      ablation_reference_only_f1: 0.760\n      ablation_surface_only_f1: 0.754\n      top_features: [hapax_ratio_0.285, ttr_0.172, entropy_mean_0.165]\n      total_records: 22920\n    result_rationale: >\n      best 档假设跨生成器泛化强健。5-gen LOGO 均值 0.81 体现了 depth signal 的 architecture-invariant \n      特性——递归生成的 distributional drift 是生成过程本身的属性，不依赖特定模型。Pythia-1B 最高因为\n      与训练集中 Pythia-2.8B 同家族共享 tokenizer/architecture bias；OLMo 最低因为 architecture \n      差异最大。家族级别 holdout 仅比 generator-level 低 ~1.5pp，说明跨家族泛化 robust。\n      per-gen std 0.032 远低于单检测器 baseline 的 per-gen variance。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Leave-One-Generator-Out F1\"\n        columns: [Held_Out_Generator, Family, Params, Macro_F1]\n        rows:\n          - [Pythia-2.8B, Pythia, 2.8B, 0.82]\n          - [Pythia-1B, Pythia, 1.0B, 0.86]\n          - [OLMo-2-1B, OLMo, 1.5B, 0.77]\n          - [Qwen3-1.7B, Qwen, 1.7B, 0.81]\n          - [Qwen3-0.6B, Qwen, 0.6B, 0.83]\n      - name: \"Table 4: Leave-One-Family-Out F1\"\n        columns: [Held_Out_Family, Macro_F1, Delta_vs_GenOut]\n        rows:\n          - [Pythia, 0.79, -0.02]\n          - [OLMo, 0.77, 0.00]\n          - [Qwen, 0.80, -0.01]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 3: Per-generator held-out F1 bar chart with CI whiskers, 展示跨生成器一致性\"\n    analysis: >\n      5-gen 评估确认 Claim 1 跨生成器泛化。Pythia 家族两个成员（1B+2.8B）不造成显著 inflation——\n      leave-one-family-out delta 仅 1.5pp。为后续 plan-016 的 9-gen 扩展奠定基础。\n\n  - name: paraphrastic_comparison\n    plan_id: plan_006\n    description: >\n      构建平行 paraphrasing chains 直接对比 continuation chains，\n      测试 attractor convergence 理论——non-paraphrastic chains 是否保留更多 depth signal。\n    expected_results:\n      paraphrastic_3class_f1: 0.74\n      paraphrastic_3class_f1_std: 0.009\n      paraphrastic_binary_f1: 0.67\n      continuation_3class_f1: 0.79\n      continuation_3class_f1_std: 0.006\n      continuation_binary_f1: 0.75\n      f1_delta_3class: -0.05\n      f1_delta_binary: -0.08\n      depth_retention_para: 0.97\n      depth_retention_cont: 0.83\n      spearman_entropy_mean_para: -0.53\n      spearman_entropy_mean_cont: -0.68\n      spearman_ttr_para: -0.44\n      spearman_ttr_cont: -0.63\n      spearman_hapax_para: -0.46\n      spearman_hapax_cont: -0.65\n      drift_direction_consistent: true\n      cross_transfer_para_to_cont_f1: 0.77\n      cross_transfer_cont_to_para_f1: 0.74\n      n_paraphrastic: 4900\n      n_continuation: 4609\n    result_rationale: >\n      best 档下 paraphrastic chains 的 depth signal 弱于 continuation 但仍可检测（F1>chance），\n      符合 attractor theory 预测：paraphrasing 的语义保持约束加速收敛（retention 97% 意味着\n      depth-4 仍有 97% 的 chains 产出合理文本），但 feature drift 幅度被压缩（Spearman ρ \n      绝对值低 ~0.15-0.20）。Crucially，drift direction 一致（同向负相关），说明 location-shift \n      机制在两种 chain 中同向作用，只是 paraphrasing 的语义锚定限制了 shift 幅度。\n      Cross-transfer F1 >0.74 说明同一特征空间对两种 chain 都有效，\n      支持统一 depth estimation framework 的叙事。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Paraphrastic vs Continuation Chains\"\n        columns: [Chain_Type, 3class_F1, Binary_F1, Retention_d4/d0]\n        rows:\n          - [Continuation, 0.79, 0.75, 0.83]\n          - [Paraphrastic, 0.74, 0.67, 0.97]\n          - [Delta, -0.05, -0.08, +0.14]\n      - name: \"Table 6: Feature Drift Comparison (Spearman ρ)\"\n        columns: [Feature, Continuation, Paraphrastic, Direction_Match]\n        rows:\n          - [entropy_mean, -0.68, -0.53, \"✓\"]\n          - [ttr, -0.63, -0.44, \"✓\"]\n          - [hapax_ratio, -0.65, -0.46, \"✓\"]\n          - [entropy_std, -0.08, -0.05, \"✓\"]\n          - [tail_decay, -0.04, -0.03, \"✓\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 4: Paired drift curves (continuation vs paraphrastic) per feature, 展示同向但幅度差异\"\n      - \"Fig 5: Cross-transfer confusion matrices\"\n    analysis: >\n      Paraphrastic chains 验证了 attractor convergence theory 的预测（semantic preservation \n      约束限制 drift 幅度），同时证明 non-paraphrastic continuation 是更优的实验设计选择，\n      因为它保留了更多可判别的 depth signal。两种 chain type 的 cross-transfer 高 F1 支持\n      统一 depth estimation 框架的可行性。\n\n  - name: finer_grained_ordinal\n    plan_id: plan_009\n    description: >\n      5-class ordinal 分类 (gen-0 through gen-4) 测试更细粒度 depth estimation 的可行性。\n    expected_results:\n      5class_macro_f1: 0.51\n      5class_f1_95ci: [0.50, 0.52]\n      5class_accuracy: 0.55\n      5class_mae: 0.65\n      3class_macro_f1: 0.79\n      delta_5class_vs_3class: -0.28\n      per_class_f1:\n        depth_0: 0.92\n        depth_1: 0.63\n        depth_2: 0.28\n        depth_3: 0.27\n        depth_4: 0.45\n      gen2_gen3_confusion_rate: 0.42\n      ordinal_methods:\n        CORAL: 0.50\n        Frank_Hall: 0.52\n        XGBoost: 0.51\n      concordance_index: 0.82\n    result_rationale: >\n      best 档下 5-class 仍然是 negative result（F1~0.51），但这完全符合 theoretical prediction：\n      attractor theory 预测 depth signal 在 ~3 classes 后饱和。gen-2 和 gen-3 基本不可分\n      （confusion rate 42%）因为 location shift 在 depth-2 后趋于 plateau——递归生成的 \n      distributional drift 存在 diminishing returns。关键正面信号：concordance index 0.82 \n      表明 ordinal ranking 仍然 well-calibrated，即使 exact classification 困难。\n      这支持 3-class 作为 practical ceiling 的 framing，同时 ordinal structure 的存在\n      validates depth as genuinely ordinal (not just categorical)。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Granularity Comparison\"\n        columns: [Granularity, Macro_F1, MAE, Concordance]\n        rows:\n          - [3-class, 0.79, 0.24, 0.87]\n          - [5-class, 0.51, 0.65, 0.82]\n      - name: \"Table 8: 5-Class Per-Depth F1\"\n        columns: [Depth, F1, Most_Confused_With]\n        rows:\n          - [gen-0, 0.92, gen-1]\n          - [gen-1, 0.63, gen-2]\n          - [gen-2, 0.28, gen-3]\n          - [gen-3, 0.27, gen-2]\n          - [gen-4, 0.45, gen-3]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 6: 5×5 confusion matrix heatmap, 展示 gen-2/gen-3 的 heavy confusion band\"\n      - \"Fig 7: F1 vs granularity curve (2-class through 5-class), 展示 3-class 后急剧衰减\"\n    analysis: >\n      5-class negative 是 theoretically predicted 且 narratively useful：它为 3-class \n      practical ceiling 提供 empirical evidence，同时 high concordance 说明 depth 确实是 \n      ordinal quantity。Paper 中作为 supporting analysis 报告，strengthen 了 framing 的理论严谨性。\n\n  - name: end_to_end_classifier\n    plan_id: plan_012\n    description: >\n      QLoRA fine-tuned Qwen3-0.6B-Base 端到端 depth classification，\n      对比 handcrafted distributional features。\n    expected_results:\n      qwen06b_5class_macro_f1: 0.59\n      qwen06b_5class_f1_std: 0.005\n      qwen06b_3class_macro_f1: 0.91\n      qwen06b_3class_f1_std: 0.003\n      pythia410m_5class_macro_f1: 0.56\n      pythia410m_3class_macro_f1: 0.87\n      per_class_f1_5class:\n        depth_0: 1.00\n        depth_1: 0.80\n        depth_2: 0.41\n        depth_3: 0.32\n        depth_4: 0.44\n      vs_xgboost_5class_delta_pp: +8.5\n      vs_xgboost_3class_delta_pp: +12.4\n      logo_generalization_f1: 0.72\n      logo_vs_within_gen_delta: -0.19\n      lora_rank: 32\n      training_epochs: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      best 档下 E2E classifier 在 within-generator CV 上大幅优于 XGBoost（+8-12pp），\n      因为 LM hidden states 能捕获 handcrafted features 无法表达的细粒度 distributional \n      shift pattern。但 LOGO generalization 仅 ~0.72（比 within-gen 低 ~19pp），说明 \n      learned representations 过拟合于 generator-specific patterns。这是 best 档的 key \n      nuance：E2E 方法在 known-generator 场景下 superior，但 handcrafted features 在 \n      unknown-generator 场景下更 robust。这 validates paper 选择 interpretable features \n      作为 primary method 的设计决策——real-world 应用面对 unknown generators，\n      interpretability + robustness > raw accuracy。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: E2E vs Feature-Based Comparison\"\n        columns: [Method, 3class_CV, 5class_CV, 3class_LOGO, Interpretable]\n        rows:\n          - [XGBoost_7feat, 0.79, 0.51, 0.79, \"✓\"]\n          - [Qwen3-0.6B_QLoRA, 0.91, 0.59, 0.72, \"✗\"]\n          - [Pythia-410M_QLoRA, 0.87, 0.56, 0.68, \"✗\"]\n      - name: \"Table 10: E2E Per-Class F1 (5-class, Qwen3-0.6B)\"\n        columns: [Depth, E2E_F1, XGBoost_F1, Delta]\n        rows:\n          - [gen-0, 1.00, 0.91, +0.09]\n          - [gen-1, 0.80, 0.63, +0.17]\n          - [gen-2, 0.41, 0.27, +0.14]\n          - [gen-3, 0.32, 0.27, +0.05]\n          - [gen-4, 0.44, 0.44, 0.00]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 8: Within-gen vs LOGO F1 对比 bar chart, 展示 E2E 泛化 gap\"\n      - \"Fig 9: t-SNE of E2E hidden states colored by depth, 展示 gen-0/gen-1 清晰分离但 gen-2+ 混叠\"\n    analysis: >\n      E2E 实验的作用是 supplementary validation：(1) 证明 depth signal 确实存在于 hidden states \n      (upper bound)；(2) 证明 handcrafted features 的 generalization 优势 justifies \n      interpretable approach 的选择。Paper 中作为 \"ceiling analysis\" 报告。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ac1c7b14-144b-4c90-8fd8-4b1f4cb72f38","total_cost_usd":0.41564700000000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":28618,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":8286,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":28618,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8286,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":28618,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":28618},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":23579,"outputTokens":25,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.023704,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":8286,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":28618,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.39194300000000004,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"ab505c5a-b7e7-47d0-85a2-228481ac0075"}
